That minimizer adapts an algorithm from RTK. Upstream's NOTICE follows
verbatim; the paths it names are relative to upstream's `crates/pi-shell`.

Upstream's NOTICE names one adapted RTK component, but upstream ports more RTK
code than that, and the RTK copyright and MIT terms below cover it as well.
RTK-derived components of this crate that upstream's NOTICE does not name
(paths relative to this crate; upstream pins no RTK commit for them):

- `src/filters/ruby.rs`: `strip_rspec_noise`, adapted from RTK's
  `src/cmds/ruby/rspec_cmd.rs::strip_noise`; `MAX_RENDERED_FAILURES`, RTK's
  `MAX_RSPEC_FAILURES` limit; and the RuboCop autocorrect summary compaction
  in `filter_rubocop`, adapted from RTK's `src/cmds/ruby/rubocop_cmd.rs`.
- `src/filters/lint.rs`: the basedpyright `strip_lines_matching` patterns and
  one inline test, re-derived from RTK's `src/filters/basedpyright.toml`; and
  the ESLint stylish "Top rules" summary, an RTK idea re-derived from ESLint's
  default text output.
- `src/filters/jvm.rs`: the Maven filters (phase detection, Surefire block
  collapse, compile, package, and quiet-mode filters) and their tests, ported
  from RTK's `src/cmds/jvm/mvn_cmd.rs`; the Gradle filters (`detect_task`,
  `filter_build_line`, `filter_test`, `filter_connected`, `filter_lint`,
  `filter_dependencies`) and their tests, ported from RTK's
  `src/cmds/jvm/gradlew_cmd.rs`; and the Spring Boot keep-list, re-derived
  from RTK's `src/filters/spring-boot.toml`. The JVM test fixtures that name
  `RtkInducedFailTest` or `com.example.rtk` appear to be RTK recordings;
  upstream does not state their source.
- `src/filters/go.rs`: the `go test` success aggregation, re-derived from
  RTK's `go_cmd`, and the test
  `looks_like_go_error_recognizes_non_location_error_shapes`, whose inputs are
  RTK's `go_cmd` inline test inputs.
- `src/defs/*.toml`: each definition whose header reads `Ported from
  https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk/blob/master/src/filters/<name>.toml` adapts
  that RTK file.

Upstream's minimizer also adapts filters, tests, and fixtures from snip, cites
snip by bare path only, and carries no snip notice. The snip notice follows
upstream's NOTICE at the end of this file.

